---
# SITEMAP INDEX. Replaces jekyll-sitemap's single flat file (the plugin is
# removed from _config.yml) so each content type reports separately in Search
# Console: "12 of 30 books indexed, 0 of 290 characters" is actionable,
# a single coverage number for everything is not.
#
# Google's own limits, for reference: 50,000 <loc> per index, 500 indexes per
# site, 50,000 URLs / 50MB per child sitemap. Nothing here is close to any of
# them, and the docs treat an index as a standard technical solution — there
# is no penalty attached to splitting.
#
# A child sitemap is listed ONLY when it has entries. Submitting an empty
# sitemap is a Search Console error, and right now authors, characters and
# categories are all deliberately unindexed, so they get no child file at all.
layout: null
permalink: /sitemap.xml
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<sitemapindex xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <sitemap>
    <loc>{{ '/sitemap-pages.xml' | absolute_url }}</loc>
    <lastmod>{{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
  </sitemap>
  {%- assign indexable_books = site.books | where: "noindex", false -%}
  {%- if indexable_books.size > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    lastmod must track when THIS SITEMAP'S CONTENTS changed, and a promotion
    changes them without touching any page's `date`: promoting seven pages
    published in July added seven <loc> entries while the newest `date` stayed
    where it was, leaving the stamp frozen and giving Google no reason to
    re-fetch the file the new URLs live in.

    So take the LATER of the two signals — newest publication, newest
    promotion. Both writers of `index_promoted` (this repo's
    scripts/promote_books_batch.py, "batch N YYYY-MM-DD", and the API's
    tools/indexing.py, "engagement YYYY-MM-DD") end the value with an ISO
    date, so the last ten characters are the date in both cases and sort
    chronologically as plain strings.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign newest_book = indexable_books | sort: "date" | last -%}
  {%- assign stamp = newest_book.date | date: "%Y-%m-%d" -%}
  {%- for b in indexable_books -%}
    {%- if b.index_promoted -%}
      {%- assign promoted_on = b.index_promoted | slice: -10, 10 -%}
      {%- if promoted_on > stamp -%}{%- assign stamp = promoted_on -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  <sitemap>
    <loc>{{ '/sitemap-books.xml' | absolute_url }}</loc>
    <lastmod>{{ stamp }}</lastmod>
  </sitemap>
  {%- endif -%}
</sitemapindex>
